1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
"Time for struts."

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,000
You hear it a lot. It's explained almost never.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Struts control how your car settles after a bump.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Worn ones keep bouncing.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
That bounce can point to longer stopping distance

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
and chewed-up tread — even when the ride feels normal.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,500
The test: push down hard on one corner. It should rebound once, then settle.

8
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,000
More bounce than that is worth checking.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Try it in your driveway. Not sure what you felt?

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Nick's Tire and Auto — link in bio.
